# Suppressions for memcheck runs of programs built for valgrind (ABLA_VALGRIND=1; tools/test-valgrind.sh passes this file).
# The runtime tells memcheck about its heap (stdlib/abla/runtime/platform/host.ab, __ablaRuntimeHostValgrind), so a program
# reports nothing of its own making; a report that is the runtime's and cannot be told apart from a program's belongs
# here, with the reason. There is none: the stack wipe and the collector's poison are skipped in these builds, and the
# allocator marks the memory it takes back from freed objects as its own.
